  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "How many pairs of positive integers $x$ and $y$ satisfy the equation $x + 2y = 2^{10}$?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$2^9-1$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$2^9$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$2^9+1$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$2^9+2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "0"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Choose $y$",
    "body": "For every $y$ the value $x = 2^{10} - 2y$ is determined, and it is positive iff $y < 2^9$. So $y = 1, 2, \\dots, 2^9 - 1$: there are $2^9 - 1 = 511$ pairs.\n\n**Answer: (A) $2^9 - 1$**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Choose $x$",
    "body": "$x = 2^{10} - 2y$ must be even and between 2 and $2^{10} - 2$: $x \\in \\{2, 4, \\dots, 1022\\}$, which is $511 = 2^9 - 1$ values, each giving one $y$.\n\n**Answer: (A) $2^9-1$**"
   }
  ],
