  },
  "grade": "11-12",
  "points": 5,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "From a regular octagon we build a square by joining the vertices as shown. If the area of the square turns out to be 2 cm², what is the area of the octagon in cm²?",
  "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2023-g1112/q21.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$1+\\sqrt2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$\\frac52$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$2\\sqrt2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "3"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$3\\sqrt2 - 1$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Use the circumradius",
    "body": "The square joins every second vertex of the octagon, so the octagon and the square have the same circumcircle with radius $R$. The square's diagonal is $2R$, so its area is $\\frac{(2R)^2}{2} = 2R^2 = 2$, giving $R = 1$.\n\nThe octagon consists of 8 isosceles triangles with legs $R$ and apex angle $45^\\circ$: area $8\\cdot\\frac12 R^2\\sin45^\\circ = 2\\sqrt2\\,R^2 = 2\\sqrt2$.\n\n**Answer: (C) $2\\sqrt2$**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Square plus four triangles",
    "body": "The octagon = the square plus 4 congruent triangles, each formed by a side of the square and the octagon vertex between its ends. With $R = 1$ as above, the square's side is $\\sqrt2$; the distance from the centre to that side is $\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}$, so each triangle has height $1 - \\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}$ and area $\\frac12\\cdot\\sqrt2\\cdot\\left(1 - \\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\right) = \\frac{\\sqrt2 - 1}{2}$. Total $2 + 4\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt2-1}{2} = 2\\sqrt2$.\n\n**Answer: (C) $2\\sqrt2$**"
   }
  ],
